.TH MOUNT 3
.SH NAME
mount - libc wrapper for a native filesystem mount
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B int mount(const char *type, const char *target, const char *source);
.SH DESCRIPTION
Requests a root-authorized native mount of type at target.  source is passed to
the registered filesystem factory and may be null.  No host filesystem is
opened and no persistence is implied.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, or -1 and sets errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
The wrapper reports the native EFAULT, EINVAL, EEXIST, ENOENT, EBUSY, EPERM,
and ENODEV errors through errno.
